# The Planetary Council's window (CouncWin, see src/ui/councwin.c): the offers the AI makes the player for his vote. On the election of a
# governor, with the player (faction 1) among the weaker so that it may not stand (votes_pivot gives the factions their votes) but its
# votes could decide between two others, a faction offers its price: with the turn poked to 100 and energy given to factions 2 and 3,
# energy credits (the first popup; the second of its choices casts the vote, and OK takes it: the energy changes hands and the player's
# vote is cast, which decides the election); then, with less energy (the price rounds to nothing) and techs to offer (give_techs_2 and
# give_techs_3 give factions 2 and 3 the first twenty), two techs, which the player takes (the New Tech window shows for each). The
# state regions are as in councwin_vote.scene, and the factions' tables (energy, techs).
# Leave time after each step; the snaps take 2 s each.
